---
import CaseStudy from '../../layouts/CaseStudy.astro';
import Figure from '../../components/Figure.astro';
---

<CaseStudy
  name="1stDibs Dealer Dashboard"
  title="1stDibs Seller Tools"
  tagline="helps sellers succeed on an online marketplace for extraordinary design objects."
  shareImage="1stdibs-dashboard-final2"
>
  <Fragment slot="meta">
    <p><strong>Year</strong> 2017</p>
    <p><strong>Role</strong> Product Designer</p>
    <p><strong>Responsibilities</strong> Product design, User research</p>
    <p>
      <strong>Collaborators</strong> Thalith N (Design), Kaley S (Research), Shir H (Product), John R (Eng), Alpere F
      (Eng), Cormick B (Eng), Stav M (Eng), Chris B (QA), and many more.
    </p>
    <p><strong>Platforms</strong> Web</p>
  </Fragment>

  <div class="intro">
    <p>
      1stdibs is an online marketplace specializing in high value luxury items such as vintage furniture, fine art, and
      design objects.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Dealer Dashboard is the hub for all seller activity but had not been updated in several years despite rapidly
      changing needs of dealers.
    </p>
    <p>
      My team was tasked with discovering what needs (both dealer and internal) had to be addressed, then launching a new
      dashboard based on our discoveries without breaking essential workflows.
    </p>
  </div>

  <Figure images={[{ name: '1stdibs-dashboard-final2', alt: 'Redesigned 1stDibs dealer dashboard' }]} lead="Dealer Dashboard." eager>
    Final designs after multiple rounds of value testing, design workshops, and QA.
  </Figure>

  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>Defining user and business goals</h2>
    <p>
      We performed generative research via design workshops and interviews with account managers, stakeholders, and
      dealers to uncover common themes in issues with the current dashboard.
    </p>
    <p>
      Sellers were most interested in how to be successful on the platform and how they were performing relative to
      other sellers. The dashboard had to answer questions such as "what immediate actions do I need to take" and "how
      can I do better on 1stdibs?"
    </p>
    <p>
      Internal users were most interested in enabling dealers to succeed on the platform with less manual intervention
      from account managers.
    </p>
  </div>

  <Figure images={[{ name: '1stdibs-dashboard-original2', alt: 'Original 1stDibs dealer dashboard' }]} lead="Original dashboard.">
    The existing dashboard was essentially a sitemap with links out to other parts of the web app.
  </Figure>

  <Figure
    images={[
      { name: 'IMG_7139-scaled', alt: 'Design workshop sticky notes' },
      { name: 'IMG_6988-1-scaled', alt: 'Design workshop participants' },
      { name: 'IMG_7140-scaled', alt: 'Design workshop sketches' },
    ]}
    lead="Design workshops."
  >
    I helped facilitate design workshops with participation from stakeholders, users, product, and engineering to
    generate insights and gather ideas from across the business before designing any flows or screens.
  </Figure>

  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>Iteration and testing</h2>
    <p>
      Alongside our researcher and other designer, I ran sessions with users to go over design concepts with
      progressively higher levels of fidelity as we crystallized what the final product would be.
    </p>
  </div>

  <Figure images={[{ name: 'value-testing2', alt: 'Two dashboard prototypes used in value testing' }]} lead="Value testing.">
    We had users interact with two different prototypes exploring differences in how the dashboard showed unresolved
    tasks, metrics, and other modules.
  </Figure>

  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>Final designs</h2>
    <p>
      The Dealer Dashboard redesign showed early signs of success at launch (based on site metrics plus feedback from
      dealers and account managers). The redesign accomplished the Dealer and Internal goals that we were building
      against, and additional iterations post-launch helped to further refine the design of this project.
    </p>
  </div>

  <Figure images={[{ name: '1stdibs-dashboard-final2', alt: 'Final dealer dashboard design' }]} tight />
  <Figure images={[{ name: 'card-documentation', alt: 'Dashboard card component documentation' }]} />
</CaseStudy>
